#
# Counter-example for the native math:MissingPreservationKind gate
# (crates/validate/src/lint.rs, check_math_missing_preservation_kind): a
# math:ProjectionRecord that enters the loss ledger declaring NO logic:preservationKind, so
# its preservation judgment is undeclared — the ledger records a projection without saying
# whether anything survived it. The native gate MUST emit math:MissingPreservationKind.
#
# Everything the other four projection gates key on is deliberately absent, so this is a
# minimal violation of exactly one rule: the record declares no preservation kind at all, so
# it is not LOSSY and neither math:UndeclaredUnsupportedConstruct nor
# math:ProjectionDroppedParameterization nor math:UnrecordedProjectionLoss can apply; its
# source is a plain math:MathematicalObject rather than a math:Distribution or a
# math:MathematicalExpression; and it declares no math:projectsConfidenceAsProbability.
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:unjudgedProjection a math:ProjectionRecord ;
    math:projectionSource ex:someObject ;
    math:projectionTargetName "OWL annotation (label only)" .

ex:someObject a math:MathematicalObject .
